00:12.640 --> 00:14.360
And it's a professor who's willing to teach

00:14.360 --> 00:17.640
and a student who's willing to learn.

00:17.640 --> 00:24.560
And so I've set up this structure around that where basically

00:24.560 --> 00:27.800
each student pays for kind of their network position.

00:27.800 --> 00:31.680
First student pays a dollar, the second student pays $2.

00:31.680 --> 00:35.000
And the goal is, if I'm a good professor over time,

00:35.000 --> 00:38.200
this network of students that I have will grow.

00:38.200 --> 00:41.480
And then the objective function of a university

00:41.480 --> 00:45.320
is to minimize the paybacks, the median payback period

00:45.320 --> 00:46.520
for students.

00:46.520 --> 00:49.360
And so basically, if I'm not teaching you stuff

00:49.360 --> 00:52.280
that it gives you leverage over your time,

00:52.280 --> 00:56.360
I'm not doing my job well as a university.

00:56.360 --> 00:58.440
